DocumentationNarrative.Body:
The same EnterpriseBIPlatform model and instance graph can move between XML, SQL, and C# workspaces without changing its meaning.

### XML workspace

The XML surface stores model and instance data in deterministic workspace files for authoring, review, branching, and merging.

### SQL workspace

`meta create --new-workspace <destination> --source-workspace <source> --with-instances --sql` creates a SQL workspace. SQL provides database-native storage, queries, and updates for large instance sets.

### C# workspace

`meta create --new-workspace <destination> --source-workspace <source> --with-instances --csharp` creates a C# workspace. Application code can work with the typed model and instance objects directly:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;

static void PrintSystems(EnterpriseBIPlatformModel model)
{
    foreach (var system in model.SystemList)
    {
        Console.WriteLine(system.SystemName + " [" + system.SystemType.TypeName + "]");

        foreach (var link in model.SystemCubeList.Where(x => x.SystemId == system.Id))
        {
            var mode = string.IsNullOrEmpty(link.ProcessingMode) ? "n/a" : link.ProcessingMode;
            Console.WriteLine("  Cube: " + link.Cube.CubeName + " (mode: " + mode + ")");
        }
    }

    foreach (var measure in model.MeasureList)
    {
        Console.WriteLine(measure.Cube.CubeName + "." + measure.MeasureName);
    }
}
```
